{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.IwahoriHecke.RMatrixSl2","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.RMatrixSl2","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BalancedGenerators","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Matrix.Basic"],"declarations":22,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.RMatrix.heckeAction_sigma_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.RMatrix.heckeAction_sigma_one","kind":"theorem","line":246,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/RMatrixSl2.lean#L246-L249","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.RMatrix.heckeAction_sigma_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.RMatrix.heckeAction_sigma_zero","kind":"theorem","line":241,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/RMatrixSl2.lean#L241-L244","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.RMatrix.heckeAction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.RMatrix.heckeAction","kind":"def","line":218,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/RMatrixSl2.lean#L218-L239","doc":"**The Hecke action of `H₃(q)` on `V^{⊗3}`.**\n\nAn honest algebra map, not a class: `σ₀ ↦ Ř₁`, `σ₁ ↦ Ř₂`, with the §7a quadratic and the\nbraid relation discharged by `isHeckeGenerator_rc1`/`rc2` and `yangBaxter`. This is the\nbraiding half of quantum Schur-Weyl at `n = 3`, realised. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.RMatrix.coxA2_symm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.RMatrix.coxA2_symm","kind":"theorem","line":216,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/RMatrixSl2.lean#L216-L216","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.RMatrix.coxA2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.RMatrix.coxA2","kind":"def","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/RMatrixSl2.lean#L212-L214","doc":"The type-`A₂` Coxeter matrix on the two generators of `H₃(q)`: the generators braid\n(`m = 3`) and neither commutes with the other. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.RMatrix.isHeckeGenerator_rc2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.RMatrix.isHeckeGenerator_rc2","kind":"theorem","line":207,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/RMatrixSl2.lean#L207-L210","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.RMatrix.isHeckeGenerator_rc1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.RMatrix.isHeckeGenerator_rc1","kind":"theorem","line":202,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/RMatrixSl2.lean#L202-L205","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.RMatrix.rc2_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.RMatrix.rc2_sq","kind":"theorem","line":192,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/RMatrixSl2.lean#L192-L200","doc":"The embedded braiding `Ř₂` satisfies the §7a quadratic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.RMatrix.rc1_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.RMatrix.rc1_sq","kind":"theorem","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/RMatrixSl2.lean#L181-L189","doc":"The embedded braiding `Ř₁` satisfies the §7a quadratic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.RMatrix.yangBaxter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.RMatrix.yangBaxter","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/RMatrixSl2.lean#L153-L171","doc":"**The Yang-Baxter equation** `Ř₁Ř₂Ř₁ = Ř₂Ř₁Ř₂` on `V^{⊗3}` — the braid relation for\nthe `sl₂` R-matrix.\n\nTogether with `isHeckeGenerator_rCheck` this is exactly what\n`QOU.IwahoriHecke.Balanced.liftBalanced` consumes, so the two of them are the whole input\nto a Hecke action on a tensor power.\n\n`q * qi = 1` is genuinely used, and only here: all 64 entries but two are ring identities\nin `q` and `qi` separately, and the two survivors differ by `(q·qi − 1)(q − qi)`. So the\nbraid relation holds for the deformed braiding **because** `qi` is `q⁻¹`, not for formal\nreasons. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.RMatrix.rc2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.RMatrix.rc2","kind":"def","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/RMatrixSl2.lean#L148-L150","doc":"`Ř₂ = id ⊗ Ř` on `V ⊗ V ⊗ V`: the braiding acting on the last two factors. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.RMatrix.rc1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.RMatrix.rc1","kind":"def","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/RMatrixSl2.lean#L144-L146","doc":"`Ř₁ = Ř ⊗ id` on `V ⊗ V ⊗ V`: the braiding acting on the first two factors. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.RMatrix.rCheck_one_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.RMatrix.rCheck_one_sq","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/RMatrixSl2.lean#L137-L140","doc":"At `q = 1` the braiding is an involution: `Ř² = 1`, the transposition relation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.RMatrix.rCheck_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.RMatrix.rCheck_one","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/RMatrixSl2.lean#L129-L135","doc":"**At `q = 1` the R-matrix IS the transposition.** The `q`-deformed braiding degenerates\nto the symmetric-group action that `QOU.MassTheory.TensorPowerTrace` computes the character\nof — so the `2^{c(σ)}` classical trace is this braiding's `q → 1` limit, checked rather\nthan assumed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.RMatrix.flip","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.RMatrix.flip","kind":"def","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/RMatrixSl2.lean#L125-L127","doc":"The flip `eᵢ ⊗ eⱼ ↦ eⱼ ⊗ eᵢ` on `V ⊗ V`, as a matrix. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.RMatrix.rCheck_sub_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.RMatrix.rCheck_sub_inv","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/RMatrixSl2.lean#L115-L121","doc":"**The skein relation for the R-matrix**: `Ř − Ř⁻¹ = q − qi`. Stated against an\narbitrary right inverse — a right inverse of `Ř` has no choice but to be the negative\ncrossing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.RMatrix.isUnit_rCheck","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.RMatrix.isUnit_rCheck","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/RMatrixSl2.lean#L110-L113","doc":"**`Ř` is invertible**, with the negative crossing `Ř − (q − qi)` as its explicit\ntwo-sided inverse. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.RMatrix.rCheck_eigen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.RMatrix.rCheck_eigen","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/RMatrixSl2.lean#L104-L108","doc":"**The eigenvalue factorisation**, from the bridge: `(Ř − q)(Ř + qi) = 0`. The symmetric\nand antisymmetric channels of the `q`-deformed braiding. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.RMatrix.isHeckeGenerator_rCheck","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.RMatrix.isHeckeGenerator_rCheck","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/RMatrixSl2.lean#L91-L102","doc":"**`Ř` is a Hecke generator** in the sense of `QOU.MathlibExt.SkeinRelation` — the\nsymmetric normalisation of AGENTS.md §7a.\n\nEverything that file proves therefore applies: `Ř` is a unit with explicit inverse\n`Ř − (q − qi)`, it satisfies the skein relation `Ř − Ř⁻¹ = q − qi`, and it factors as\n`(Ř − q)(Ř + qi) = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.RMatrix.rCheck_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.RMatrix.rCheck_sq","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/RMatrixSl2.lean#L78-L89","doc":"**The R-matrix satisfies the §7a Hecke quadratic relation.**\n\n`Ř² = (q − qi) Ř + 1`, so `Ř` has eigenvalues `q` and `−qi`. This is the statement that\nmakes the braiding a *Hecke* braiding rather than merely an invertible operator, and it is\nwhere `q * qi = 1` is used: without it the diagonal entries give `q² ≠ (q − qi)q + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.RMatrix.rCheck_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.RMatrix.rCheck_apply","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/RMatrixSl2.lean#L73-L76","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.RMatrix.rCheck","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.RMatrix.rCheck","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/RMatrixSl2.lean#L56-L69","doc":"**Jimbo's `Ř`-matrix** for the fundamental of `U_q(sl₂)`, on `V ⊗ V` with\n`V = Fin 2 → R`, indexed by `Fin 2 × Fin 2`.\n\nOn basis vectors:\n\n* `Ř (eᵢ ⊗ eᵢ) = q · eᵢ ⊗ eᵢ` — the symmetric channel, eigenvalue `q`;\n* `Ř (e₀ ⊗ e₁) = e₁ ⊗ e₀ + (q − qi) · e₀ ⊗ e₁`;\n* `Ř (e₁ ⊗ e₀) = e₀ ⊗ e₁`.\n\nAt `q = qi = 1` the middle coefficient vanishes and this is the flip (`rCheck_one`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}